      "body": "## Overview\n\nFix the `dots` tool parser's non-streaming path dropping the text after the last\n`<dots_function_call>` block, so streaming and non-streaming return the same\n`content`. Related to #56270 (merged as 81f7c69), which fixed the same class of\nbug in the DeepSeek-V3 parser.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Non-streaming `extract_tool_calls` now keeps the preamble plus the text after\n  the last `</dots_function_call>` marker (previously only the preamble).\n- Streaming and non-streaming return identical `content` for the same output.\n- Tool-call extraction, schema coercion, unknown-tool handling, and the\n  `if not tool_calls: content=model_output` early return are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nReproducer (stream=false):\n\n    let me check the weather.<dots_function_call><invoke name=\"get_weather\"><parameter name=\"city\">Paris</parameter></invoke></dots_function_call>It is 30 degrees.\n\n- before: `content = \"let me check the weather.\"` (drops `It is 30 degrees.`)\n- after : `content = \"let me check the weather.It is 30 degrees.\"` (== streaming)\n\nNew regression tests in `tests/tool_parsers/test_dots_tool_parser.py`:\n`test_non_stream_keeps_text_after_tool_call` and\n`test_stream_keeps_text_after_tool_call`. Both use the same input and assert the\nsame `content`.\n\n    VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu python -m pytest -q tests/tool_parsers/test_dots_tool_parser.py\n    # => 12 passed\n\nThe non-streaming test fails without the fix:\n\n    assert 'let me check the weather.' == 'let me check the weather.It is 30 degrees.'\n\n## Details\n\n**Root cause.** `extract_tool_calls` (line 250) set\n`normal_text = model_output[:marker_index].strip()`, i.e. only the preamble.\n`extract_tool_calls_streaming` accumulates `normal_parts` for text outside\nsuccessfully parsed blocks, including the trailing text.\n\n**Fix.** Mirror #56270: keep the preamble plus the text after the last end\nmarker.\n\n    tool_calls_end = model_output.rfind(self.tool_call_end_token)\n    normal_text = model_output[:marker_index]\n    if tool_calls_end != -1:\n        normal_text += model_output[tool_calls_end + len(self.tool_call_end_token):]\n    normal_text = normal_text.strip()\n\n**Limitation (same scope as #56270).** Text *between* multiple\n`<dots_function_call>` blocks is still not kept by the non-streaming path; the\nfix only restores the trailing text.\n\n**Not a duplicate.** #56270 fixed the same class in the DeepSeek-V3 parser and\ndoes not touch Dots. #55199 touches only the Qwen3 Parser Engine. #60516 touches\nthis file but only for null/boolean coercion.\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:**&#8203; Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:**&#8203; Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:**&#8203; Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:**&#8203; Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
